<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  RBM mode's gear of Commander Battle's Empire troop classes (cb_mpclassdivisions_empire.xml), read by
  CommanderBattle/RbmLoadouts.cs (its header has the format). Light mode keeps the classes' mp_ gear and never reads
  this file. Singleplayer items only, as RBM retunes them (RBM.Multiplayer loads SandBoxCore's items and RBM's item
  files in multiplayer): no mp_ items, no looter or nord items.
  - One Class per MPHeroClass id, the general's class included. Hero: the commander's gear. Troop: the bots' rosters;
    a bot draws every slot from a random roster, so each slot holds the same kind of item in every roster and the
    rosters only vary the looks (armour and helmets of one tier). Setup N: the class's N-th weapon setup perk, slot
    for slot as its AlternativeEquipmentOnSpawn effects (no id empties the slot).
  - Slots as the mp_ characters: Item0 main weapon, Item1 shield (or arrows, bolts), Item2 sidearm, Item3 the
    archers' targe (a pavise with the crossbow) or the skirmishers' second bundle of javelins. Cape holds RBM's
    shoulder pieces. Mounted classes have a horse and a harness in the hero and in every roster; foot classes none.
  - Gear tiers: light = levy (gambesons and padded armour, a real helmet); medium = legionaries and equites (mail);
    heavy = palatine guards and cataphracts (lamellar and scale, closed helms, the best weapons).
  - Empire doctrine: kite shields for the infantry of every weight, shielded archers with middling composite bows,
    cataphracts with a targe and a mace. Sidearm rule (README): spears, the menavlion, lances and javelins keep the
    sidearm (gladius or spatha, maces for the cavalry); sword setups clear it; archers keep theirs.
  - The Empire's own SP lances (empire_lance_*) couch: RBM's couched lance pieces and weapon descriptions are loaded
    in multiplayer, so the mp_western_lance stand-in is not needed here.
  - Javelins: northern_javelin_1_t2, the Javelin-template bundle RBM gives its Imperial infantry, two bundles as the
    mp_ skirmishers. Not the pila (imperial_throwing_spear_*): TwoHandedPolearm crafts, wielded as spears, one per slot
    and not thrown from the saddle.
  - Shields: the plain ids, not RBM's _shoulder copies its troops carry (same stats, but their holsters come from
    RBM's holster loader, which multiplayer doesn't run). The cataphract targe is battania_shield_targe_a, RBM's
    battania_shield_targe_a_cataphract_shoulder without the holster. So is the archers' targe: RBM's battania_targe_b
    sits on RBM's forearm holster, and the engine throws spawning it.
  Seeded from RBM's troop overhaul (RBMCombat_unit_overhaul.xml):
    levy spearman       imperial_infantryman (helmets: the trained infantryman's and the mp_ levy's kinds)
    legionary           imperial_veteran_infantryman (menavlion: imperial_menavliaton)
    palatine guard      imperial_legionary, imperial_elite_menavliaton (heavy menavlion, armour variant)
    levy archer         imperial_archer (helmets: imperial_trained_archer; crossbow: crossbow_i, RBM levy bolts)
    sagittarius         imperial_veteran_archer (crossbow: imperial_sergeant_crossbowman)
    courser             imperial_vigla_recruit (lance and mace from imperial_heavy_horseman's kind)
    equite              imperial_equite (armour), imperial_heavy_horseman (lance, shield)
    cataphract          imperial_cataphract
    bucellarius         bucellarii (bow, arrows, horse) in imperial_vigla_recruit's light armour
    strategos, guard    imperial_elite_cataphract, the strategos with the plumed helmet and legionary cape
-->
